{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "e1664347-fa21-475f-9da5-72b3f781481b",
    "name": "e-commerce API · products",
    "description": "The product endpoints of the e-commerce learning repo, served by `ProductController` at the `products` root.\n\n**Before running:** start the API with `pnpm start:dev`, which brings up Postgres, Mongo and Mailpit through Docker Compose and then boots Nest on the port in `.env` (3000 by default).\n\n**Variables:** `baseUrl` and `accessToken` come from the shared **e-commerce (local)** environment; select it before running. Only `productId` stays a collection variable, because nothing outside this collection reads it.\n\n**Auth model:** `JwtAuthGuard` is registered as `APP_GUARD`, so creating, replacing and deleting a product need a bearer access token; the two GETs are `@Public()`, since browsing a catalogue must not require an account. The collection sets bearer `{{accessToken}}` at the collection level and overrides the public GETs to No Auth; run Login in the auth-context collection to populate the token.\n\n**Run order:** `Create product` stores the new id in the `productId` collection variable, and every later request reads it. Run it first, or set `productId` by hand.\n\n**Status codes:** 400 comes from the validation pipe and carries no `code` field, while 422, 404 and 409 come from the typed exception filters and carry a stable `code`. Validity is decided before existence, so a request that is both invalid and aimed at a missing id answers 422, not 404.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
